      "title": "Origami for School Age Kids",
      "description": "<p>Please join us as we learn 3 origami projects. Each project will be demonstrated step-by-step. Origami paper is provided. No registration required, just come and learn to fold origami! This program is for children currently in grades Kindergarten through 8th grade. Parents and caregivers are welcome to join and help your child (children).</p>\n<p>Generously sponsored by the Friends of Cupertino Library.<br></p><p>For accessibility accommodations (ex. ASL), please fill out the online form at <a href=\"https://sccld.org/accessibility/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-auth=\"NotApplicable\" id=\"OWA5e41f473-2c03-8a9a-5ea1-2cc34f0e05c7\" data-linkindex=\"0\" title=\"https://sccld.org/accessibility/\">sccld.org/accessibility</a> 7+ days prior to the event. If you need assistance with the form, speak with a staff member at your local library, call <a href=\"tel:(408) 540-3947\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-auth=\"NotApplicable\" data-linkindex=\"1\" title=\"tel:(408) 540-3945\">(408) 540-3947</a>7, or email us at <a href=\"mailto:ask@lib.sccgov.org\" id=\"OWA3a96a92d-c453-b9ed-9996-3fe02a0b57c5\" title=\"mailto:ask@sccl.org\" data-linkindex=\"2\">ask@lib.sccgov.org</a>.<br></p>",
